%% Figure 20-3 — Detection, policy, and enforcement for one protected effect.
%% Message: the detector only raises a finding. The policy engine decides, and
%% the Tool Gateway enforces before anything commits, whether or not the
%% detector noticed the attack.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Agent as Agent Runtime
    participant Det as Content detector
    participant Pol as Policy Engine
    participant App as Approval Service
    participant Tool as Tool Gateway
    participant Sys as System of Record

    Agent->>Det: proposed action + content
    Det->>Det: inspect untrusted content
    Det->>Pol: finding (risk label), action, subject, resource
    Pol->>Pol: evaluate policy with the finding as one input
    alt not permitted
        Pol-->>Agent: refuse, nothing dispatched
    else permitted
        alt requires human approval
            Pol->>App: request approval
            App-->>Pol: signed approval, bound to this proposal
        end
        Pol-->>Tool: authorized invocation
        Tool->>Tool: enforce exact resource, check idempotency ledger
        Tool->>Sys: commit once
        Sys-->>Tool: receipt
        Tool-->>Agent: effect record + evidence
    end
